# Line-ending policy.
#
# Git for Windows defaults to `core.autocrlf=true`, which rewrites every text
# file to CRLF on checkout. That made the verification gates depend on the state
# of a developer's working copy rather than on the committed content: on a fresh
# clone or in a git worktree, `prettier --check` reported *every* frontend file
# as unformatted, because Prettier expects LF.
#
# The defect was invisible in place — the working copy here was written by tools
# in LF and never re-checked-out — and only appeared when an isolated worktree
# was checked out from the same commit. `vector-tools repair lane --gate
# format-check` is what surfaced it.
#
# Normalising to LF everywhere makes a checkout reproduce the committed bytes.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Patch files are applied verbatim; rewriting their line endings breaks them.
*.patch -text
*.diff -text

# Binary assets must never be converted.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.icns binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.ttf binary
*.exe binary
*.dll binary
*.msi binary
*.gguf binary
*.gz binary
*.zip binary
